## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to perform multi-word arithmetic with pure bitwise/arith operations, handling carry without branches.

## Key Concepts
- 128-bit arithmetic via two 64-bit halves
- Carry propagation using unsigned overflow properties
- Branchless computation

## Code Example
```c
void add128(uint64_t a_hi, uint64_t a_lo, uint64_t b_hi, uint64_t b_lo, uint64_t *out_hi, uint64_t *out_lo){
  uint64_t lo = a_lo + b_lo;
  uint64_t carry = (lo < a_lo);
  uint64_t hi = a_hi + b_hi + carry;
  *out_hi = hi;
  *out_lo = lo;
}
```

